Origin:
vcmbox(4) on the Raspberry
Pi 5 under ACPI, where the mailbox device comes from our firmware
(netbsd/firmware/vc-mailbox.diff). The real-time clock the firmware keeps
(GET/SET_RTC_REG, register 0 = seconds since 1970) becomes the system
clock chip: our firmware stops serving the EFI clock at runtime, so that
the kernel alone owns the mailbox. The firmware's throttling flags
(GET_THROTTLED) become envsys indicators: under-voltage and throttled, now
and since boot, with a log line on the first under-voltage.

--- sys/arch/evbarm/rpi/rpi_vcmbox.c.orig
+++ sys/arch/evbarm/rpi/rpi_vcmbox.c
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@ __KERNEL_RCSID(0, "$NetBSD: rpi_vcmbox.c,v 1.8 2021/03/08 13:53:08 mlelstv Exp $
 #include <sys/systm.h>
 #include <sys/sysctl.h>
 
+#include <dev/clock_subr.h>
 #include <dev/sysmon/sysmonvar.h>
 
 #include <arm/broadcom/bcm2835_mbox.h>
@@ -62,6 +63,18 @@ struct vcmbox_clockrate_request {
 	struct vcprop_tag end;
